==Battleground==
*3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 22 seconds<sup>660f</sup>, delay 4~6 seconds<sup>120f~180f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn after 166.67 seconds<sup>5,000f</sup>, delay 19.33~22 seconds<sup>580f~660f</sup>.
*12 [[Mr. Angel]]s spawn after 140 seconds<sup>4,200f</sup>, delay 2.67~5.33 seconds<sup>80f~160f</sup>.
*3 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 16~18 seconds<sup>480f~540f</sup>.
*1 [[Le'noir]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.
*1 [[Dober P.D]] spawns after 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.
*1 [[Berserkory]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*3 [[Two Can]]s spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage consists of heavy-hitting enemies whose [[Wave Attack]]s are capable of destroying your backline. The first and biggest threat in this stage is Dober P.D, who has 1.2 million health and only two knockbacks. You will want to make sure he stays far away from your [[Cat Base]], as if he starts to attack it you won't be able to push him back before he shreds your backliners. It is highly recommended to bring [[Battle Items#Sniper the Cat|Sniper the Cat]] if you are unable to kill Dober P.D in time. The other enemies can be an issue too; Berserkory's Wave Attack covers the entire battlefield and Two Can has very high damage output.

[[Cat Units]] who can attack from afar are very helpful here, as they can push out enough damage before taking any themselves. You do not want to bring generalist meatshields like [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Wall Cat]] as the damage they absorb will cause Wave Attacks to appear more often.

===Recommended Units===
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - At level 28, Awakened Bahamut can deal exactly enough damage to kill each Gory Dark in one attack. To get the most damage output, summon him when the Gory Darks get close to your Cat Base. Awakened Bahamut can also tank a hit from Le'noir, so you can use him to finish the stage quicker.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - Having a short recharge time and [[Massive Damage]] to [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] enemies, Courier is capable of completely shredding both Two Can and Berserkory. His [[Long Distance]] range allows him to consistently deal damage to his respective target even if close-range enemies get in the way.
*[[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] - Its [[Wave Shield]] ability completely nullifies all Waves on the battlefield, rendering Two Can and Berserkory nearly useless. You may want to have spare cash to make sure he has as much uptime as possible.
*[[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] - Not only can Ring Girl deal Massive Damage to Two Can and Le'noir, she has generally good health and attack power. If you have a good defensive holdup, she can provide extra support damage.

